<title>HONG KONG: Exceptional boosts Stelux interim profit.</title>
<headline>Exceptional boosts Stelux interim profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   8.7	vs 5.4</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.0	vs 1.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  43.88    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    81.33    vs 50.47</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,046.11 vs 929.37</p>
<p>    Company name		 Stelux Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 27-30</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   February 26</p>
<p>NOTE - Stelux Holdings engages in property, retailing and trading, and manufacturing of watch components.</p>
<p>It proposed a bouns issue of warrants in the proportion of one warrant for every five shares held.</p>
<p>Exceptional gain represents foreign exchange gain on Swiss Francs convertible notes and profit on sale of land and building.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
